 { White has an extra pawn, but his passed pawn on c5 is firmly blocked by the enemy knight. Kashdan found a strong idea, in the spirit of 'activity above material'. } 1. { -KEY- } Nd4 $1 { It is worth a pawn to eliminate that knight. } ( { In contrast, } 1. Kf3 $6 Kg6 { , followed by ...Kf6, would increase Black's chances of survival. } ) 
Nxd4 ( { Or } 1... Rc8 2. Nxc6 Rxc6 3. Kf3 { followed by Ke4-d5. } ) 
2. exd4 Rxd4 3. c6 Rd8 4. Kf3 $1 { King first! } ( { The impulsive } 4. c7 $2 { fails after } Rc8 5. Kf3 a4 $1 6. Ke4 a3 7. Kd5 a2 { with a draw. } ) 
a4 ( { Or } 4... Kg6 5. Ke4 Kf6 6. c7 Rc8 7. Kd5 { and the king reaches c6. } ) 
5. Ke4 a3 6. Ke5 { The king is finally ready to assist the passed pawn. } Rd3 ( { The threat of } 6... Rd3 6. c7 { and Kd6-d7 next forces Black to desperate action. } ) 
7. c7 a2 8. Rxa2 Rc3 9. Kd6 Rd3+ 10. Kc6 Rc3+ 11. Kb7 Rb3+ 12. Ka8 Rc3 13. Ra7 $1 ( { Preparing a bridge. In view of } 14. Kb8 { next, Black resigned. } ) 

