1... { -KEY- } Rh1 $2 ( { Despite the minus pawn, Black would have had reasonable drawing chances in the rook ending arising after } 1... Bxc3 $1 2. Kxc3 h5 { , gaining space on the kingside, while keeping the rook in a restrictive location. But Botvinnik prefers to keep the minor pieces on the board, which yields White a golden opportunity. } ( { Or } 2... g5 { , but not } Rh1 $2 3. Kd4 $1 { with the double threat of 4. Ke5 and 4. Rc7+ } ) 
 ) 
2. Ne4 $1 { Petrosian exploits the moment to improve his knight and king, unworried about the loss of the h-pawn. } Rxh2 3. Kd4 Kd7 ( { Or } 3... Rxg2 4. Rc7 Kd8 5. Rxh7 { followed by Ke5, with a huge advantage - 'Bulletin'. } ) 
4. g3 $1 ( { Avoiding } 4. g4 $6 h5 $1 5. g5 h4 { with counterplay. } ) 
Bb4 5. Ke5 $1 { The king has found a path along f6-g7. } Rh5+ ( { Obviously, the restrictive } 5... Be7 { now fails to } 6. Rd2  { and 7.Kxe6 } ) 
6. Kf6 Be7+ 7. Kg7 $1 e5 { The picture has changed completely since the initial diagram - material is equal, but White's activity is overwhelming. } 8. Rc6 $1 { Preparing Kf7 and Re6 in order to deflect the bishop from either of the crucial d6- and f6-squares. } Rh1 9. Kf7 Ra1 ( { The passive } 9... Rh5 { can be met by } 10. g4 ( 9... Ra1 9. a5 $5 { opening a new front on the queenside, is interesting as well; } ) 
Rh4 11. Re6 Bd8 12. Rd6 { - 'Bulletin'. } ) 
10. Re6 $1 Bd8 ( { a) Very passive; but the rook ending arising after } 10... Bc5 11. Nxc5 bxc5 12. Rxe5 Rxa4 13. Rxc5 { should also win for White, whose king remains extraordinarily placed on f7. } ) 
 ( { b) On the other hand, } 10... Bb4 { permits } 11. Nf6 Kc8 12. Rxe5 { when } Rxa4 { unfortunately runs into } 13. Re4 $1  { with } 14. Nd5 { next - 'Bulletin'. } ) 
11. Rd6+ ( { The materialistic } 11. Rxe5 Rxa4 12. Kg7 { was possible too, but Petrosian prefers a different plan, based on the gradual restriction of the enemy pieces. } ) 
Kc8 ( { If } 11... Kc7 $2 { then } 12. Ke8 { and the bishop is trapped. } ) 
12. Ke8 $1 Bc7 13. Rc6 Rd1 { On the defensive. } ( { a) } 13... Rxa4 $2 { was impossible due to } 14. Nc3 { followed by 15 Nd5 - 'Bulletin' } ) 
 ( { b) While after } 13... Kb7 14. Ng5 $1 { , Black still can't play } Rxa4 { in view of } 15. Ne6 Bb8 16. Nd8 Ka8 17. Rc8 { followed by Nc6, with a tragicomical position. } ) 
14. Ng5 Rd8+ 15. Kf7 Rd7+ ( { There was the threat of } 14... Rd7+ 14. Rxc7 ) 
16. Kg8 { In view of the rapid collapse of his kingside, Black resigned. } 
 1-0

